{"id":"CAP-021-01","type":"finding_candidate","title":"Current DSH GAT behavioral baseline is an uncommitted working-tree state","content":"The selected DSH baseline is rooted at commit aeedf19995babaa28e35ca84624baff18a77a7d8 but all relevant gat-core/tools/profile/web feature files are modified or untracked. Synchronization must pin file hashes and cannot cite the commit alone as the behavioral revision.","status":"captured","discovered_at":"2026-09-26","candidate_kind":"tool_gotcha","suggested_target":"wiki_reference","improvement_scope":"project","reusable":true,"source_refs":[".ai-work/workspaces/hoinv/TASK-20260926-exec-021/dsh-baseline-sha256.txt"]}
{"id":"CAP-021-02","type":"finding_candidate","title":"DSH GAT Web mount and component contracts drift","content":"Current DSH gat-web mount removes approveMission/importApprovedPlan injections while the identical TeamActionInjected interface still requires them; its component test also omits required enabled/enable fields. Blind baseline copying would create type or test drift.","status":"captured","discovered_at":"2026-09-26","candidate_kind":"spec_impl_drift","suggested_target":"future_backlog","improvement_scope":"project","reusable":true,"source_refs":["/home/hoinv/deepseek-harness/packages/experimental/gat-web/src/client/mount.ts","/home/hoinv/deepseek-harness/packages/experimental/gat-web/src/client/TeamAction.tsx","/home/hoinv/deepseek-harness/packages/experimental/gat-web/tests/team-action.client.spec.tsx"]}
{"id":"CAP-021-03","type":"finding_candidate","title":"Simple-mode approval shortcut is not authenticated mission authorization","content":"Current simpleMode skips the legacy plan approval gate and current mission creation uses a Lead Agent credential without host-attested HUMAN provenance. Treating this as mission-as-authorization would allow the model to self-authorize. The frozen target requires a host-attested exact mission revision and revalidation at effect/wake boundaries.","status":"captured","discovered_at":"2026-09-26","candidate_kind":"spec_impl_drift","suggested_target":"future_backlog","improvement_scope":"project","reusable":true,"source_refs":["docs/GAT_MEMBER_BINDING_CONTRACT_FREEZE.md","packages/tools/src/index.ts","packages/core/src/mission-board.ts"]}
{"id":"CAP-021-04","type":"finding_candidate","title":"Installer structural verification does not prove lockfile installability","content":"The supported-target installer completed structuralVerification PASS while a subsequent pnpm install --frozen-lockfile rejected the installed gat-tools manifest because the compatibility lockfile lacked new yaml and dsh-llm specifiers. Compatibility verification must include a frozen dependency install or equivalent lockfile/package consistency check.","status":"captured","discovered_at":"2026-09-26","candidate_kind":"tool_gotcha","suggested_target":"future_backlog","improvement_scope":"project","reusable":true,"source_refs":["compatibility/dsh-0.1.5-rc.2/patchset/after/pnpm-lock.yaml","packages/tools/package.json","installer/verify.mjs"]}
{"id":"CAP-021-05","type":"tooling_opportunity_candidate","title":"Compatibility lock normalization must preserve live workspace profile links","content":"Letting pnpm normalize file: profile dependencies converted workspace-facing link resolutions into packaged file snapshots. Those snapshots were created before build and did not expose later gat-core lib output to the Web profile scaffold. The deterministic generator now adds only the missing importer dependencies while preserving local link resolutions.","status":"captured","discovered_at":"2026-09-26","candidate_kind":"aiws_system_improvement","suggested_target":"future_backlog","improvement_scope":"project","reusable":true,"source_refs":["scripts/generate-compatibility.mjs","compatibility/dsh-0.1.5-rc.2/patchset/after/pnpm-lock.yaml","verification/web/gat-agent-team-panel.e2e.ts"]}
{"id":"CAP-021-06","type":"tooling_opportunity_candidate","title":"Installer verifier must build the native helper before GAT unit tests","content":"The installer verifier linked JavaScript dependencies but removed build outputs and launched GAT tests before producing native/system's host addon. The resulting broad core failures were environmental rather than product assertions. Verification now runs build:native-system before the unit suite.","status":"captured","discovered_at":"2026-09-26","candidate_kind":"aiws_system_improvement","suggested_target":"future_backlog","improvement_scope":"project","reusable":true,"source_refs":["installer/verify.mjs"]}
{"id":"CAP-021-07","type":"tooling_opportunity_candidate","title":"Opt-in Team browser verification must cross the enable boundary","content":"The installed Web E2E opened the Team panel and immediately asserted an active roster, but synchronized GAT is session opt-in. The fixture must explicitly click the enable action and snapshot the resulting built-in fallback roster; otherwise a timeout or stale one-member golden masks the actual lifecycle contract.","status":"captured","discovered_at":"2026-09-26","candidate_kind":"aiws_system_improvement","suggested_target":"future_backlog","improvement_scope":"project","reusable":true,"source_refs":["verification/web/gat-agent-team-panel.e2e.ts","verification/web/task.expected.md"]}
